    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math> is the good leaving group, i.e is the weakest nucleophile among the given options</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cl</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>OC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><msub><mi>OCOCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the rate of reaction is faster, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>.</p>",
